-- title:
--   Smooth chart algebras commute with base change ℤ₍ₚ₎→ A
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and write $R=\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ (Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$) and $x\in F_0$, and assume that `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg R F₀ {x}`, the subalgebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over $R[x]=$ `Algebra.adjoin R {x}`, is a smooth $R$-algebra. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and finite dimension over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $K'$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $A$ be a domain with an $R$-algebra structure and an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$ compatibly with $R\to L$, and assume that an element of $L$ is integral over $R$ exactly when it lies in the image of $A$; let $K'$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K'$. Let $x'\in K'$ have image `coeffEmb L x` in $L((q))$. Then there is an isomorphism of $A$-algebras $$A\otimes_R \mathrm{chartAlg}(R,F_0,\{x\}) \;\cong\; \mathrm{chartAlg}(A,K',\{x'\})$$ onto the elements of $K'$ integral over $A[x']$, which sends $1\otimes b$ to the element of $K'$ whose image in $L((q))$ is `coeffEmb L b`.
--
--   This is the assertion that, in the presence of smoothness, the integral closure defining a chart of the two-chart integral model commutes with the base change $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}\to A$, $F_0\to L\cdot F_0$. Applied to the two charts ($j$ and $j^{-1}$) it feeds the good-reduction statement for the two-chart integral model of $X_1$, namely [`ModularCurve.XOne.smooth_toBase_and_isIntegral_pullback_twoChartIntegralModel_x1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOne.smooth_toBase_and_isIntegral_pullback_twoChartIntegralModel_x1).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algEquiv_tensorProduct_chartAlg_laurentBaseChange_of_smooth.lean

